  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improving Food Security through support of Sustainable Livelihoods in Central and Western Equatoria</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aims to improve the livelihood status of some of the most vulnerable people living in the targeted communities in Yei Diocese, South Sudan. The long term aim is to provide the beneficiaries (both returnees and those affected by drought) with the inputs and skills to increase their food security, and lift themselves out of poverty.
At the end of the 22 month project it is envisioned that the project will address the food security needs of the most vulnerable in the targeted communities.  1000 households will demonstrate a significant improvement in their food security. This will be measured by conducting a baseline survey within the first month of the project, using indicators that will then be monitored throughout the duration of the project.  There will also be an additional 200 households that will receive support in other livelihood approaches such as fishing. The project will also address some of the water, sanitation and hygiene needs of the 1000 households in the targeted communities. This will in turn contribute to an overall improvement of their health and wellbeing by the end of the project.</narrative>
  </description>
